 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.78,
   "text": "This question comes from N. Murdock, who was thinking about how the three wise men in",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 3.78,
   "end": 6.92,
   "text": "the Christmas story followed a star to Bethlehem where they found the baby Jesus.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 7.36,
   "end": 10.84,
   "text": "The question is, what if you did walk toward a known star at a fixed speed?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 11.26,
   "end": 12.56,
   "text": "What path would you trace on the earth?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 13.0,
   "end": 15.14,
   "text": "Sirius is the brightest star in the sky other than the sun.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 15.5,
   "end": 19.38,
   "text": "If the wise men left Jerusalem on December 25th, 1 A.D. and walked toward Sirius day",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 19.38,
   "end": 22.76,
   "text": "and night, even when it's below the horizon, this spiral is the path they follow over",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 22.76,
   "end": 23.16,
   "text": "the surface.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 23.66,
   "end": 26.76,
   "text": "The size of the spiral is determined by how far a person can walk in half a day.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.12,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.002
  },
  {
   "start": 26.76,
   "end": 30.8,
   "text": "If we allow a little theological confusion and assume that the wise men can walk on water,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 31.14,
   "end": 34.58,
   "text": "they'll eventually wind up going in an endless circle 30 kilometers in diameter around",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 34.58,
   "end": 35.2,
   "text": "the South Pole.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 35.62,
   "end": 36.74,
   "text": "But let's be a little more realistic.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 37.22,
   "end": 40.16,
   "text": "The wise men are hardly going to walk toward the star while it's behind the earth.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 40.58,
   "end": 43.64,
   "text": "Let's assume they only walk toward the star while it's in the sky and the sun",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 43.64,
   "end": 45.84,
   "text": "has set, but they can still walk on water.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 46.18,
   "end": 48.8,
   "text": "In that case, their path actually takes them through Bethlehem.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 49.24,
   "end": 52.16,
   "text": "If they don't stop there, after a few years they wind up circling Botswana.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 52.7,
   "end": 56.4,
   "text": "These paths are calculated using, among other things, PIE-FM, which provides tools",
   "avg_logprob": -0.142,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.02
  },
  {
   "start": 56.4,
   "end": 59.06,
   "text": "for determining the historical positions of astronomical objects.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 59.66,
   "end": 62.12,
   "text": "It's tricky to figure out exactly what the wise men would have been following.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 62.46,
   "end": 65.18,
   "text": "There aren't very many good astronomical candidates for the star of Bethlehem.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 65.68,
   "end": 68.8,
   "text": "Chinese records don't show a supernova at the right time, and none of the other obvious",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 68.8,
   "end": 69.94,
   "text": "candidates really check out.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 70.24,
   "end": 73.56,
   "text": "And furthermore, there's a lot of historical and theological debate over Jesus' date,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 73.82,
   "end": 74.76,
   "text": "and even year of birth.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 75.24,
   "end": 78.52,
   "text": "The paths in this video are all calculated for a somewhat arbitrary departure date from",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 78.52,
   "end": 80.64,
   "text": "Jerusalem of December 25th, 1 A.D.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 80.9,
   "end": 84.08,
   "text": "Different departure dates would lead to different paths, but the overall picture would be",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  },
  {
   "start": 84.08,
   "end": 84.76,
   "text": "roughly the same.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.138,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.006
  }
 ],
